{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And they saw.</b> In a prophetic vision, like \"I saw YHWH sitting on a throne\" (1 Kings 22:19; 2 Chronicles 18:18)." "The Gaon [Saadia] said that סַפִּיר לָבָן — the seeing of it is לִבְנַת הַסַּפִּיר, and it is nothing but red. The proof is that the usage of the language is to duplicate the meaning in different words, and behold it is written: \"Her princes were purer than snow, whiter than milk\" (Lamentations 4:7) — and behold the meaning is duplicated; \"Their body was redder than coral\" — לְפִנִּים סַפִּיר גְּזָרָתָם (ibid.) — and behold סַפִּיר is like פְּנִינִים. Furthermore, if לִבְנַת הַסַּפִּיר is whiteness, what is the meaning of saying כְּמַעֲשֵׂה? It should have said כְּמַרְאֵה. The correct view is that לִבְנַת is from the root לָבָנָה, like חֶשְׁכַת מַיִם (Psalms 18:12) from the root חֹשֶׁךְ (Genesis 15:12). And so לִבְנַת הַסַּפִּיר is like the sapphire stone that Ezekiel saw in the prophetic visions, which is the likeness of a throne." "And the meaning of וּכְעֶצֶם הַשָּׁמַיִם לָטֹהַר is in place of לִבְנַת הַסַּפִּיר, and it is the רָקִיעַ, which is like the appearance of ice that is stretched over the heads of the living creatures that Ezekiel saw. And behold it is written: \"And they saw the Elohim of Israel,\" and there it is written: \"This is the living creature that I saw under the Elohim of Israel\" (Ezekiel 10:20) — for he took a short route, for it is under the רָקִיעַ, and it too is under the throne, and all is under the revered Name."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {1 "Where Ibn Ezra quotes Lamentations 4:7, his text reads לפנים where the standard Masoretic text has גְּעָלִים; rendered hyper-literally as it stands in his quotation."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:38:07.832596017Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}